  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shriram Expanding Access to Finance for Micro, Small, and Medium-Sized Enterprises Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Asian Development Bank (ADB) loan gives Shriram Finance Limited (SFL) much-needed longer-tenor funding to expand its capacity to provide financing to micro, small, and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs) in India for their purchase of electric vehicles, low-emission vehicles compliant with Bharat Stage VI (BS-VI) standards, and for general business loans, including those which are women-owned MSMEs (WMSMEs) and those located in lagging states. MSMEs in India remain underserved and face several challenges, including the lack of financial flexibility and limited access to formal modes of financing, resulting in heavy reliance on informal lenders.</narrative>
  </description>
